 "text": "9/29/26, 10:15 AM\n\nDunning\n\nYou can create payment reminders or dunning letters and send them to your business partners, to alert them of overdue payables\nand to request payment.\n\nYou can print correspondence either using the Correspondence component or directly by using the application forms that you\nhave defined in the Print Workbench.\n\nIn addition to the features of the standard delivery, you can realize industry-specific dunning activities.\n\n1 Note\nIndustry Component Utilities (IS-U)\n\nYou can dun budget billing requests as well as open items. The dunning run can create lock documents automatically (see\nDisconnection/Reconnection of a Utility Installation). You can postprocess the dunning-relevant data manually in the dunning\nproposal.\n\nIndustry Component Telecommunications (IS-T)\n\nYou can postprocess the dunning-relevant data manually in the dunning proposal. If receivables have reached a specific\ncollection step, you can lock the contract account or the service for a business partner automatically in the dunning activities\nrun (see Lock Services Using SAP RM-CA and SAP CRM).\n\nIndustry Component Insurance (FS-CD)\n\nThe following dunning procedure types are supported:\n\ne Individual Dunning Notices\n\nIn an individual dunning notice, all items in a contract are considered independently of one another. This means that you\ncan have several dunning procedures for one contract.\n\ne Collective Dunning\nIn acollective dunning notice, all items in a contract are dunned with one dunning procedure.\ne Multi-Collective dunning\n\nMultiple collective dunning can, in contrast to collective dunning, contain several collective dunning notices for one\nbusiness partner/insurance object relationship in parallel.\n\ne Contract Dunning\n\nIn a contract dunning notice, only one current dunning procedure exists at any one point in time. This refers to the\noldest item.\n\ne Account Dunning All items due for dunning for a contract account are dunned on a cross-contract basis for account\ndunning.\n\nThe dunning procedures to be used are determined in the dunning proposal run and saved in the item.\n",
